text:
Maya (Docs): drafting a compact 'migration cribsheet' for the v1->v2 sunset email. goal: single-page CTA with exactly two runnable snippets (JS + Py), one minimal runtime fallback, and 4 quick gotchas. keeping it extremely short for customers to copy/paste.
Jon (SDK): Love the cribsheet idea. please include the literal call mapping table and one-line on streaming framing. customers keep pasting the old `models.invoke` call and getting confusing errors.
Maya (Docs): Will add. Planned JS snippet (old vs new):
```js
// v1
const r = await client.models.invoke({ model: 'rwd-lite', input: prompt })
// v2
const r = await client.responses.create({ model: 'rwd-lite-v2', input: prompt })
```
Maya (Docs): Planned Python snippet:
```py
# v1
r = client.models.invoke(model='rwd-lite', input=prompt)
# v2
r = client.responses.create(model='rwd-lite-v2', input=prompt)
```
Pri (Product): Add one small, copyable fallback customers can use during rollout. non-opinionated. also want a 1-line instruction to configure alias fallbacks before cutoff.
Maya (Docs): Adding minimal fallback example (purely illustrative):
```js
// minimal runtime fallback
try {
  return await client.responses.create({ model: 'rwd-lite-v2', input })
} catch (e) {
  return await client.responses.create({ model: 'rwd-lite-compat', input })
}
```
Jon (SDK): Also add a tiny streaming note: "If you used streaming in v1, switch to responses.stream and parse framed JSON chunks (for await ...)." Put a link to the streaming migration guide.
Maya (Docs): will do. Gotchas (4 bullets) I'll include in the cribsheet body: 1) call rename: models.invoke -> responses.create, 2) streaming frame change, 3) param rename (max_tokens -> max_output_tokens) in some SDK helpers, 4) older SDKs: header name differences and upgrade suggestion.
Pri (Product): timeline: we want the cribsheet merged and linked in the deprecation email next Tue. Can you create runnable snippet files and a smoke test so CI protects us from broken examples?
Maya (Docs): yes  adding runnable files under docs/snippets/migration/ and a small smoke test that runs node and python examples. will open a draft PR and tag @Jon and @Pri for review. PR link will appear here.
ci-bot: Reminder: docs CI will block merges if snippet smoke tests fail. Please ensure snippet files are executable and include minimal package.json/test harness. :robot_face:
Jon (SDK): I'll review the snippets quickly once the PR is up. If you want I can drop a tiny test harness to validate both JS & Py examples.
Maya (Docs): thanks  aiming to open PR today and merge by Monday to hit the email schedule. tagging @Jon and @Pri for final thumbs.
Jon (SDK): +1
Pri (Product): +1
Maya (Docs): great, posting PR once ready.
